# Browser
# CR 508.8 skips the declare blockers step only when no creature attacks. Bot1's Llanowar Elves attacks Bot2, who has
# Benalish Hero to block with and declares no blockers. The declare blockers step still happens, and once the (empty)
# declaration is made the active player gets priority in it (CR 509.4, 117.3a): Bot1 casts Giant Growth on the
# unblocked Elves before combat damage, which deals 4 (Bot2 to 16).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Giant Growth
Forest x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Benalish Hero
Plains x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Benalish Hero.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
? Step = Blockers
? Combat.Blocks.Count = 0
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Your declare blockers step
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Giant Growth.Cast(Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 4
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot1.Graveyard = Giant Growth
Bot2.Battlefield.Benalish Hero.Tapped = false
